# Car Physics Sim

A browser-based 2D car driving sim with real gearbox/RPM physics, tire slip, handbrake drifting, and per-car synthesized engine sound — pick from real cars and drive with WASD.

## Live Demo

[https://ahmedthe13thuser.github.io/Drift-King/]

## Screenshot

![A preview of my drifting game](Screenshot.png)

## Features

- Gearbox-driven RPM, rev limiter, and drivetrain physics
- Speed-dependent steering and tire slip, boosted by the handbrake for drifting
- 9 selectable cars, each with its own weight, power, gearing, and grip
- Real-time synthesized engine audio per car — cylinder count, intake/exhaust waveguide length, and muffler config all vary by engine

## Running Locally

This is a static site (HTML/CSS/JS, no build step, no dependencies) — any local web server works.

1. Clone the repo:
   ```bash
   git clone [https://github.com/ahmedthe13thuser/Drift-King.git]
   cd Drift-King
   ```
2. Serve the folder. Pick one:
   - **VS Code**: install the "Live Server" extension, right-click `index.html` → "Open with Live Server"
   - **Python 3**: `python3 -m http.server 8000`, then open `http://localhost:8000`
   - **Node**: `npx serve`, then open the printed URL
3. Open the served URL in your browser and drive.

> Opening `index.html` directly via `file://` won't work for the engine sound — AudioWorklet modules need to be served over http(s). Use one of the local server options above.

## Controls

| Key       | Action               |
| --------- | -------------------- |
| `W`       | Throttle             |
| `S`       | Brake                |
| `A` / `D` | Steer                |
| `Space`   | Handbrake            |
| `↑` / `↓` | Shift gear up / down |

## Credits

Engine audio is generated with [engine-sound-generator](https://github.com/Antonio-R1/engine-sound-generator) by [Antonio-R1](https://github.com/Antonio-R1), a physically-modeled car engine sound synthesizer built on the Web Audio API (MIT licensed, included in this repo under `engine-sound-generator/`). See that project's README for the underlying research it's based on.
